/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T12:08:51-07:00","id":1518772,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.backerkit.com/c/onyx-path/trinity-continuum-aegis-tabletop-roleplaying-game\" target=\"_blank\">Saga has begun!!!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T20:11:07-07:00","id":1518802,"title":"","content":"The cover looks spiffy.<br /> <br /> <br /> And put me down as another hoping for future sourcebooks looking at Egypt, Persia, and China.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T00:13:17-07:00","id":1518816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1514796-trinity-aegis-kickstarter?p=1518802#post1518802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The cover looks spiffy.<br /> <br /> <br /> And put me down as another hoping for future sourcebooks looking at Egypt, Persia, and China.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want those books too. And toss in a sourcebook on the ancient Celts too. India and Southeast Asia seem like good candidates as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T08:08:15-07:00","id":1518824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1514796-trinity-aegis-kickstarter?p=1518816#post1518816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want those books too. And toss in a sourcebook on the ancient Celts too. India and Southeast Asia seem like good candidates as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Maybe the Mayans as well. (I'd have to check the timeline.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T11:53:23-07:00","id":1518836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1514796-trinity-aegis-kickstarter?p=1518824#post1518824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. Maybe the Mayans as well. (I'd have to check the timeline.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure, but if not the Mayans then the Toltecs. The Polynesian islanders seem like a viable choice as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T16:41:51-07:00","id":1518854,"title":"","content":"Poking about, I find that the Greek Iron Age/Homeric Age/Dark Age is roughly 1100 - 800 BC and the Archaic Period is 800 to 500 BC.<br /> <br /> This period is the time of the Heraclids (descendants of Heracles) and Perseides (of Perseus and Andromeda) and the start of the Greek Poleis/city states. <br /> <br /> In Egypt, this is the Third Intermediate Period (1077 - 664 BC) and the Late Period (664 - 332 BC). The Intermediate period has a divided Egypt along with various foreign dynasties from Libya and Nubia. The Late Period is a revival period, with an increased interest in neighboring regions including Greece. <br /> <br /> In the Middle East, we have the Neo-Assyrian Empire (911 - 609 BC) and Neo-Babylonian Empire (626 - 539 BC). This period apparently includes the conquest of the Kingdom of Judea, the destruction of Solomon's Temple in Jerusalem, and the start of the Babylonian Captivity. It also includes the growth of the Phoenician trading empire and the founding of Carthage (814 BC). And just a little north is the Urartu kingdom(s), who appear to be descended from the Hittites. <br /> <br /> With the Celts in Central Europe, you've got the Hallstatt culture centered in what is now Austria and Switzerland (1200 - 450 BC). This is, apparently, when you start to see the development of what would eventually become the leadership castes of warriors, druids, and bards known to the Roman era. By the later part of this period, the culture has spread to Britain, France, and Iberia. <br /> <br /> Further north, you get the Nordic Bronze Age cultures (@2000 - 500 BC), who apparently had relatively strong trade connections with the Mycenaean Greeks. This predates what we usually think of as Nordic religion/mythology, and while we don't know much about it, there seems to be some fragmentary evidence of a sun cult and an earth goddess cult. <br /> <br /> Moving east, you have the Medes is what we think of as Persia (who will eventually end up conquering much of the Middle East under their later dynasties). <br /> <br /> In India, you have the Vedic Age (@1500 - @500 BC). <br /> <br /> Southeast Asia and Indonesia are part of the Maritime Jade Road with coastal China. <br /> <br /> In China, you have the Shang (1600 - 1046 BC) and Zhou (1046 - 256 BC) periods. The Zhou sees the start of chariot warfare and government bureaucracy. <br /> <br /> Into the Pacific, Melanesia and Micronesia are settled, but not what we think of as Polynesia. <br /> <br /> And then in the Americas, you have the Preclassical Mayan culture (2000 BC - 250 AD) and the Olmecs (1500 - 400 BC).<br /> <br /> And looping back around to Africa, there's evidence of copper and iron working cultures in the Niger River region and Cameroon. This is also the period of the Bantu language expansion. <br /> <br /> This isn't an exhaustive list of what's going on, but hits a lot of the high notes. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T21:17:13-07:00","id":1518868,"title":"","content":"Discords have decoded 'LION' symbol on Sky Chariot falling into Mt. Olympus - it's written in Classical Greek<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: